    "created_at": "2026-11-11T17:54:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-11T17:54:18Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the report, @linuxguy123 - here is what we found. Draft fix: #875.\n\n**1. Why Setup2 can't reuse Setup1's stock.** In Setup2 the part is held turned 90° about X (\"turned X -90°\" in Part alignment) - the plate stands on its edge there, while Setup1 holds it flat as modelled. Creating a setup never turns the part by itself (with \"Carry stock and WCS over\" it copies Setup1's alignment), so the turn came from an alignment change on Setup2. The stock simulation keeps the machined stock as a grid of vertical columns. It can carry that grid into another setup only when the part is flipped over X or Y or turned about Z, because those keep the tool pointing straight down the same columns. Standing the plate on its edge would mean rebuilding the grid sideways and losing detail, so the app refuses instead of guessing. That part works as intended for now. If both setups hold the plate the same way, the stock carries over fine (a test now checks this).\n   Carrying stock into a side-on setup is planned work: **#874** (it waits on the new stock engine, #637).\n   **What to do today:** choose \"Its own stock\" for Setup2, or hold the part in Setup2 the same way as in Setup1 (flipped or turned about Z also works).\n\n**2. The 35-second \"freeze\" in the log.** That line came from the file dialog. The open-file dialog is modal, and our slow-frame timer counted the time you spent picking the STEP file as app work. Nothing was computing for 35 s. The timer now leaves dialog time out: **#872**.\n\n**3. \"Furniture\" and the red message.** \"Furniture\" was our internal word for a setup's stock, work offset and fixtures, and it should never have reached the screen. The radio now reads \"Active setup - new operations go into it, and the Stock and Work offset pages edit it\". The red message now names the turn (\"'Setup2' holds the part turned X -90°, Y 0°, Z 0° from how 'Setup1' holds it\") and says what to do: **#873**.\n\nSub-issues: #872 (dialog time in the slow-frame log), #873 (wording), #874 (carry through side-on turns). #875 fixes #872 and #873. #866 stays open for the side-on carry (#874).\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
